      "value": "> the texture being 16k was the main reason for the avatar failing to load.\n\nI think you're correct - 16k is an extremely large resolution for an avatar texture! This texture will take up a very large amount of VRAM, and VRChat may prevent your avatar from being loaded to protect users.\n\nConsider restructuring your texture to be more efficient. It can fit into a 4096x4096 resolution without losing any data. This will also allow Unity to compress your texture's download size - and you can even enable mimaps to increase the clarity of your texture.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
